  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The Sodick LN2W post (`assets/posts/sodick-ln2w.cps`) now writes the control's wire offset when the stream has a `COMP` record. Both \"control\" and \"wear\" compensation are accepted.\n- The post writes `G41` / `G42 Hnnn` on its own line, after the pass's C word and before the lead-in. This is the own-line form from the machine owner.\n- H is the pass number from `H001`. The first skim is `H002`. A pass above `H999` is refused by name.\n- The first pass must be on `C001`, because `C001` always goes with `H001` (the owner). Another condition is refused by name.\n- A later pass writes the condition that the operation states. The post does not compute `C00n`.\n- `G40` goes on the lead-out move, in the same block as its `G01`.\n- `G29` is not written.\n- A comment line before each `G41` / `G42` names the register, its condition and the stated radius. It tells the operator to set the register at the control.\n- A new shared prelude helper, `crates/post/src/post/wire_offset.rs`, holds the law that other wire dialects can use (the owner's request on #4076):\n  - a lead-in or a lead-out that has no length, or is shorter than the offset radius, is refused by name (one rule, `_woLead`, for the two moves);\n  - an arc lead-in or an arc lead-out is refused by name;\n  - a change of side while the offset is on is refused;\n  - a section that ends with the offset on is refused.\n- The engine publishes `programOffsets` before `onOpen`. It has one entry for each section: `\"control\"`, `\"wear\"` or `\"\"`. The post writes its header and its section notes from it:\n  - An offset program has the header line `WIRE OFFSET G41 G42 IS USED IN EACH SECTION THAT NAMES AN H REGISTER - ...`. It does not say \"NO WIRE OFFSET\".\n  - A section on the control's offset says that the path is the part contour without the kerf. Its side note and its condition note do not say that the kerf is in the path.\n  - A wear section keeps its kerf notes, because its path is the wire-centre path.\n  - A section without a `COMP` record keeps its wire-centre notes.\n- The `C000` approach option together with an offset is refused by name.\n- Without a `COMP` record, the output does not change. The Mark 21 post (`sodick-wire.cps`) does not change.\n- `assets/posts/AGENTS.md` and `docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md` describe the offset form, the helper, the refusals, `programOffsets` and the pins.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe post refused every `COMP` record (#1498 decision), so an LN2W program with control-side offset could not post. This is a new capability, so the type is `feat`.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins in `crates/post/tests/sodick_ln2w/offset.rs` (binary `script_sodick_ln2w`):\n\n- `offset::a_control_side_wire_offset_posts_in_the_owners_form`\n- `offset::a_lead_in_shorter_than_the_wire_radius_is_refused_by_name`\n- `offset::an_arc_lead_in_or_lead_out_is_refused_by_name`\n- `offset::a_first_offset_pass_on_a_condition_other_than_c001_is_refused_by_name`\n- `offset::a_section_that_ends_with_the_offset_on_is_refused_by_name`\n- `offset::the_approach_condition_with_a_wire_offset_is_refused_by_name`\n- `offset::a_lead_out_shorter_than_the_wire_radius_is_refused_by_name` (round 2: no length, 0.01 mm, and exactly the radius posts)\n- `offset::the_notes_of_an_offset_program_state_the_offset` (round 2: header and section notes; control, wear, and no `COMP`)\n- `offset::a_change_of_side_while_the_offset_is_on_is_refused_by_name` (round 2)\n- `offset::a_pass_above_h999_is_refused_by_name` (round 2)\n\nThe first six failed on unchanged code. Each saw the old refusal \"control-side wire offset (G41/G42 H) is not supported\".\n\nThe old pin `a_control_side_wire_offset_is_refused_by_name` (in `pins.rs`) is removed. It pinned the behaviour that this issue changes.\n\nMutation checks (guard disabled, pin run, guard restored, pin run again):\n\n| Guard | Mutated | Restored |\n|---|---|---|\n| lead-in length | red | green |\n| arc lead-in | red | green |\n| arc lead-out | red | green |\n| offset on at section end | red | green |\n| C001 on the first pass | red | green |\n| C000 approach with offset | red | green |\n| G40 on the lead-out | red | green |\n| H from the pass number | red | green |\n| lead-out length (`_woLead` call for the cancel move removed) | red | green |\n| notes from `programOffsets` (`offsetMode` and `offsetProgram` return \"no offset\") | red | green |\n| change of side (`if (st.active)` changed to `if (false)`) | red | green |\n| H999 limit (`pass > 999` changed to `pass > 99999`) | red | green |\n\nGates on the final head `430c41c52`, against `upstream/main` dc3679fb5:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 212 steps, 0 failed. This includes `script_sodick_ln2w`, `script_sodick_wire`, `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work` and `wire_post`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: 72 steps, 0 failed (22.9 min).\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `git diff --stat upstream/main...HEAD -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\" examples/catalog` is empty. The quick gate ran the three `example_catalog*` suites, and the `wire_post` suite ran the LN2W goldens. They are byte-identical.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The app does not emit a `COMP` record for a Wire Contour. Its wire stream still states compensation off. So the app goldens of the square and the 2-axis part with offset on (issue item 4) are not in this PR. The post side is pinned on synthetic streams. The app side (a compensation mode for Wire Contour, a part-contour path, and the wire laws on it) is the follow-up issue #4134. This PR uses `Fixes #4076` because #4134 carries that remaining item.\n- The output is not verified on a control.\n- The owner stated the length rule for the lead-in only. The lead-out uses the same rule. The decision record says so.\n- A section that has a control pass and a wear pass gets the \"control\" section notes. The note before each `G41` / `G42` states the pass's own mode. This mix is not pinned.\n- The light lane was not run in this round.\n- The three non-blocking notes of the review (a `sectionOk = false` on the \"a move changes Z\" refusal, the length of the offset note, a pin for an offset that engages after a plain cut) are not changed.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #4114 touches `crates/post/src/post/mod.rs`, a different module line. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #4075 (taper) will stack on this branch.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/4076-ln2w-wire-offset.md`.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: The Sodick LN2W post writes the control's wire offset (G41 / G42 Hnnn before the lead-in, G40 on the lead-out) and refuses a lead-in or a lead-out shorter than the offset radius.\n\nFixes #4076\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
